{"nodes": [{"id": "registry_types_mockregistryentry", "label": "MockRegistryEntry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L36-64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_mockregistry", "label": "MockRegistry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_mockregistrydraftentry", "label": "MockRegistryDraftEntry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L88-94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_mockregistrydraft", "label": "MockRegistryDraft", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L97-99", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_checkedmockregistry", "label": "CheckedMockRegistry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L123-125", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_checkedentry", "label": "CheckedEntry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L137-141", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_checkedentryoptions", "label": "CheckedEntryOptions", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L144-148", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_checkedoptions", "label": "CheckedOptions", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L158-165", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "registry_types_two_statement_declaration", "label": "Two-statement registry declaration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L69-125", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One annotation cannot both supply contextual types on the way in and read a concrete schema back out: annotating the thunk as () => Promise<z.ZodType> collapses the dynamic import's .then type parameter to z.ZodType, so every override check passes vacuously against unknown. So the draft type leaves schema untyped while typing options, and a second `satisfies CheckedMockRegistry<typeof registry>` statement reads each entry's real schema back up out of the literal. Two statements because the check must name the table's own type and a declaration cannot refer to itself."}, {"id": "registry_types_lazy_schema_thunk", "label": "Schema as a lazy thunk", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L36-49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An entry holds a function resolving a schema, never a schema value, so a build-time config (next.config.ts) can import the host's table to derive interception rules while reading only the keys - pulling in no application module, no zod and no faker. Laziness is runtime-only: TypeScript still resolves the dynamic import's type statically, which is what lets CheckedMockRegistry check overrides against the schema."}, {"id": "registry_types_planned_entry", "label": "planned entry marker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L55-63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A planned key is a design sketch for an endpoint that does not exist yet, so the drift test asserts it resolves to no route.ts; the day the real route lands the test fails and forces the entry to be promoted or deleted, which is what stops a stale mock silently shadowing a working endpoint."}], "edges": [{"source": "registry_types_mockregistry", "target": "registry_types_mockregistryentry", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L67", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "registry_types_mockregistrydraft", "target": "registry_types_mockregistrydraftentry", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L97-99", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "registry_types_checkedmockregistry", "target": "registry_types_checkedentry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L124", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "registry_types_checkedentry", "target": "registry_types_mockregistryentry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L140-141", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "registry_types_checkedentry", "target": "registry_types_checkedentryoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L140", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "registry_types_checkedentryoptions", "target": "registry_types_checkedoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/mock/src/registry/types.ts", "source_location": "L147", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "registry_types_checkedmockregistry", "target": "registry_types_mockregistrydraft", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score